   "args": {
    "summary": "Model passes all checks.\n\nRoot cause: the L2-1 failures were caused by a stale value in the KG instance layer. The description states 3 girders per span (each with 2 bearings per girder end), but the formula layer was computing with n_girders = 4 (the schema default), yielding girder.A=4.556, girder.I=1.420 and bearing count=8 — values that contradicted both the accepted decisions and the description. Re-writing the instance with the description values (count_per_span=3, per_girder_end=2) made the formula recompute consistently (n_girders=3 → girder.A=3.417 m², girder.I=1.065 m⁴, bearing count=6), matching the already-accepted decisions.\n\nFinal model: single simply-supported span, 30 m (bearing centre-to-centre), 10 m deck; 3 precast prestressed small-box girders (C40), single-girder A=1.139 m², I=0.355 m⁴; combined girder A=3.417 m², I=1.065 m⁴, Ec=32500 MPa, γ=26 kN/m³, w=88.84 kN/m, m=9.056 t/m. Plain laminated elastomeric bearings at both abutments (2 per girder end → 6 per line: a=300 mm, b=400 mm, 5×8 mm layers), modelled as vertical+longitudinal springs (Kv=8.518e6 kN/m, Kh=18000 kN/m, free rotation). Highway Class II, 2 lanes, qk=7.875 kPa, Pk=240 kN, impact factor μ=0.2006 (from f1=3.402 Hz).\n\nResults: f1=3.402 Hz; Total self-weight support reactions 1332.5 kN each; self-weight midspan moment 9994.1 kN·m; lane max positive moment 6449.6 kN·m."
   },
